# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# Production requirement summary:
#   REQUIRED for basic production   -> Core, Database, Auth
#   REQUIRED for real AI            -> AI_PROVIDER=openai + OPENAI_API_KEY
#   REQUIRED for real WhatsApp      -> META_APP_ID, META_CONFIG_ID,
#                                      WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN, WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET
#   REQUIRED for a durable queue    -> REDIS_URL (a real hosted Redis, not localhost)
#   OPTIONAL                        -> Payments, Email, Object storage
# Without the "required for X" sections, that feature runs its existing,
# honestly-labeled demo/sandbox path instead of failing — see
# src/config/env.ts#integrationReadiness.

# --- Core (REQUIRED) ---
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
WEB_APP_URL=http://localhost:5173

# --- Database (PostgreSQL) (REQUIRED) ---
# Local: postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/loopwave
# Or a free-tier hosted instance (Neon, Supabase, Railway, RDS, etc.)
# IMPORTANT: if this endpoint goes through PgBouncer/connection pooling in
# transaction mode (Neon's default "-pooler" endpoint, Supabase's pooler,
# RDS Proxy in transaction mode, etc.), append &pgbouncer=true. Without it,
# Prisma's prepared-statement caching can misfire under concurrent requests —
# queries silently return stale or wrong results (observed here as spurious
# foreign-key violations under test-suite load). Not needed for a direct,
# unpooled Postgres connection.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/loopwave
# Prisma's schema.prisma references DIRECT_URL directly, so it must always be
# set to *some* valid postgresql:// URL or `prisma migrate`/`generate` will
# fail to resolve it. On plain local/RDS Postgres, just repeat DATABASE_URL's
# value here. On Neon specifically: DATABASE_URL is the pooled (-pooler)
# endpoint for the app at runtime; DIRECT_URL is the same connection without
# "-pooler" in the host, used only by `prisma migrate` (pgbouncer's
# transaction pooling can't hold the advisory lock migrations need).
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/loopwave

# --- Auth ---
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
# Only JWT_ACCESS_SECRET signs anything (short-lived access tokens). Refresh
# tokens are opaque random strings, SHA-256 hashed before storage — there is
# no separate refresh-token signing secret to configure.
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=replace-me-64-char-hex
JWT_ACCESS_TTL=15m
JWT_REFRESH_TTL=30d
COOKIE_DOMAIN=localhost

# --- Redis (background jobs, BullMQ) ---
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# --- WhatsApp Business Platform (Meta) — official Cloud API only ---
# One Meta App serves every tenant's Embedded Signup. META_APP_ID/
# META_CONFIG_ID are not secret (they ship in the frontend bundle to init
# the Facebook JS SDK). WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET/WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN are
# backend-only. Leave all of these unset to run WhatsApp connect in an
# honest "Meta App not configured" state instead of a fake success.
META_APP_ID=
META_CONFIG_ID=
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=
WHATSAPP_API_VERSION=v21.0

# --- AI provider (abstracted — see src/integrations/ai.adapter.ts) ---
AI_PROVIDER=demo
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Payments (Stripe is the only implemented provider — see server/src/integrations/payments.adapter.ts) ---
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# From the Stripe Dashboard webhook endpoint you point at {WEB_APP_URL's API}/api/billing/webhook.
# Subscribe it to: checkout.session.completed, invoice.paid, invoice.payment_failed,
# customer.subscription.updated, customer.subscription.deleted
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Email ---
EMAIL_PROVIDER=demo
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=Loopwave <notifications@loopwave.demo>

# --- Object storage (S3-compatible: real AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, DigitalOcean
# Spaces, Backblaze B2) — used for WhatsApp media (Inbox attachments, campaign
# header media). Leave all of these blank and the app honestly reports "Media
# storage is not configured" wherever media is sent, instead of faking success.
#
# For real AWS S3: set STORAGE_REGION/STORAGE_BUCKET/STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID/
# STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY and leave STORAGE_ENDPOINT blank (AWS resolves its
# own endpoint from the region; setting a custom endpoint for AWS forces
# path-style addressing, which is deprecated and breaks in some regions).
#
# For R2/Spaces/B2 (or any other S3-compatible provider): also set
# STORAGE_ENDPOINT to that provider's endpoint URL.
STORAGE_ENDPOINT=
STORAGE_REGION=
STORAGE_BUCKET=
STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Same credentials under AWS's own naming convention — accepted as a fallback
# if STORAGE_REGION/STORAGE_BUCKET/STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID/STORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
# are left blank. Set one set or the other, not a mix of both for the same value.
AWS_REGION=
AWS_S3_BUCKET=
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- Field-level encryption for stored integration/WhatsApp secrets ---
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-me-32-byte-hex
